//? Title: The Kalman family: actual estimates, covariance and approximation limits
//? Subtitle: Original linear/nonlinear simulations, RTS smoothing, sampled filters and fixed-gain trackers
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
State estimation combines a dynamics model with noisy observations. We begin
with one scalar prediction/correction captured at native API boundaries, then
retain the original full family comparison: linear KF and RTS smoothing, EKF/UKF
nonlinear estimation, information form, ensemble and particle methods, and
alpha-beta/alpha-beta-gamma trackers. All original observation sequences, model
parameters and seeds remain. Actual finite trajectories and error diagnostics
replace cached accuracy claims; covariance statements are separated from
realized-error comparisons and nonlinear approximations are not assumed to
succeed.
)

\toc

> See one native prediction and correction first

Take prior mean0 and variance4, F=H=1, process variance1, measurement variance3
and observation2. Prediction increases variance to5. The scalar gain is
analytically5/8; correction gives mean1.25 and variance1.875. The program
captures actual prior, predicted and corrected states around native calls,
rather than replaying equations for the displayed result. Its diagram is the
causal information flow, not a smoother or an iteration trace.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kalman_stage.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/filter/kalman_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <algorithm>
#include <numeric>
#include <cmath>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto s = dm::filter::kalman_tiny_step();
    std::print("| actual stage | mean | variance |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| prior | {} | {} |\n| predicted " "| {} | {} |\n| corrected | {} | {} |\n",
               s.prior.x[0], s.prior.P[0][0], s.predicted.x[0],
               s.predicted.P[0][0], s.filtered.x[0], s.filtered.P[0][0]);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("prior", {0, 0},
           std::format("Prior mean {}\nvariance {}", s.prior.x[0],
                       s.prior.P[0][0])).node("predict", {5, 0},
                                              std::format(
                                              "Actual prediction\nvariance {}",
                                              s.predicted.P[0][0])).node(
        "update", {10, 0},
        std::format("Actual correction\nmean {} / variance {}", s.filtered.x[0],
                    s.filtered.P[0][0])).node("sensor", {5, 4},
                                              "Observation 2\nmeasurement variance 3").edge("prior", "predict").edge("predict", "update").edge("sensor", "update").save_svg("build/kalman_stage.svg");
}
